{
  "summary": "Adds an Events IPC interface over Cap'n Proto that provides a single, ordered, pull-based stream of block and mempool notifications. External clients can subscribe to block connections and disconnections, as well as mempool additions and removals, with optional serialized payloads and configurable byte-bounded buffering. It also updates internal mempool tracking to report the mempool sequence number when transactions are removed due to being mined in a block.",
  "problem": "Existing ZMQ notification mechanisms have significant gaps for external applications: block notifications skip intermediate blocks during rapid updates or IBD, transaction notifications do not distinguish mempool acceptance from transactions included in blocks, and sequence notifications omit payload data and block-inclusion removal reasons. Furthermore, ZMQ buffer limits count messages rather than total bytes, risking unbounded memory consumption when full blocks are queued.",
  "evidence": [
    "Cites long-standing user pain points regarding inability to distinguish mempool entry from block inclusion in PR #19462, PR #23624, and PR #7753 (\"pain point of https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/19462#issuecomment-658304417, https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/23624#issue-1065790580 and https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/7753\")"
  ],
