  },
  "scope_notes": "Because libmultiprocess currently lacks native mapping from std::variant to Cap'n Proto unions, the PR manually implements union conversions in events-types.h.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Bitcoin Core PR #36985 adds an Events IPC interface that streams block and mempool events in a single ordered, byte-bounded stream. It addresses persistent gaps in ZMQ notifications, which skip intermediate blocks, cannot differentiate between mempool admissions and block transactions, and cannot stream ordered payloads alongside sequence updates. The author cites unresolved ZMQ pain points from PRs #19462, #23624, and #7753. The change also modifies mempool removal tracking so that removals caused by block inclusion retain their sequence numbers.",
